.TH "OPS\-DEPLOY" 1 "" "ops" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ops\-deploy \- ship a service
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBops deploy\fR [flags] <service> [replicas]
.SH DESCRIPTION
This command is in beta: it may change in a minor release.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fI<service>\fR
the service to ship (length 2..63)
.sp
The service to ship, by its registry name.
.sp
Names are lowercase.
.br
2 to 63 characters; matches \(ga^[a\-z][a\-z0\-9\-]*$\(ga
.TP
\fI[replicas]\fR
how many copies (>= 1)
.br
at least 1
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-port\fR \fIint\fR
listen port (default 8080) (1..65535)
.sp
The port the service listens on.
.br
between 1 and 65535
.TP
\fB\-\-ratio\fR \fIfloat64\fR
traffic share (> 0, <= 1) (experimental)
.br
greater than 0 and at most 1
.TP
\fB\-\-step\fR \fIint\fR
rollout step (multiple of 5)
.br
a multiple of 5
.TP
\fB\-\-tag\fR \fI[]string\fR
a label (1..5 values, length <= 10, repeatable)
.br
1 to 5 values; each value at most 10 characters; several values per occurrence,
separated by ","; repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fIduration\fR
how long to wait (>= 1s, < 1h)
.br
at least 1s and less than 1h
.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-env\fR \fImap[string]string\fR
extra environment (<= 8 values, repeatable)
.br
at most 8 values; repeatable
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
print help
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
say more (repeatable)
.br
repeat to count: \-vvv
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fIstring\fR
when to color (default auto) [auto|always|never]
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
\fB0\fR
shipped
.TP
\fB4\fR (rejected)
the cluster refused it
.br
See \fIhttps://example.com/ops/rejected\fR.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBops\fR(1)
